<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>User interface for the prompt-conditioned, pairwise preference study.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.5 </span>Additional Metric: Open-Vocabulary Detection</h3>

<div id="A4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As a complementary metric, we assess <em id="A4.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">subject presence</em> with OWL-V2 open-vocabulary detection <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Minderer et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. For each prompt, we pass the subject strings as class queries and count an image as correct if <em id="A4.SS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">all</em> subjects are detected at least once. We report the fraction of images meeting this criterion.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Results for test-time control and fine-tuned models are shown in <a href="#A4.T7" title="In D.5 Additional Metric: Open-Vocabulary Detection ‣ Appendix D Hyperparameters ‣ Optimal Control Meets Flow Matching:A Principled Route to Multi-Subject Fidelity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tables</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> and <a href="#A4.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ D.5 Additional Metric: Open-Vocabulary Detection ‣ Appendix D Hyperparameters ‣ Optimal Control Meets Flow Matching:A Principled Route to Multi-Subject Fidelity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>. Both control algorithms increase subject presence over the base model. However, OWL-V2 is blind to attribute leakage and subject numerosity (it does not verify attributes or counts), so we exclude it from the main evaluation and report it only as a supportive metric here.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T7" class="ltx_table">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure ltx_flex_table">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
